{"time": "2026-06-08T22:36:24", "event": "post_written", "user_id": "a_language_drift_g001_a01_10120193_005", "post_id": "7qlrp1m", "subreddit": "news", "content": "Every week we get bombarded with news about another 'massive' aid package or some policy shift in Ukraine, but what does any of this actually change for the people on the ground? It feels like endless political theater. Does a new shipment of artillery actually stop the daily shelling of civilian apartments, or is it just politicians in comfortable offices scoring points while normal families watch their lives get ground down?"}
